<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Ghassanid Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">220 CE – 638 CE (approx.) · capital Jabiyah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Christian Arab allies of Byzantium who guarded the desert frontier of Syria and patronised Miaphysite Christianity until the Islamic conquests.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ghassanids">Ghassanids</a> were an Arab tribe said to have migrated from south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> to the Syrian desert margins, traditionally in the 3rd century. Around 500 they became Roman federates, and in 529 the emperor Justinian made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-harith-ibn-jabala">al-Harith ibn Jabala</a> supreme phylarch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>, giving the family authority over the allied tribes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire's</a> eastern frontier.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ghassanid rulers led mobile cavalry against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lakhmid-kingdom">Lakhmid Kingdom</a>, ally of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, and policed the desert routes. They were committed Miaphysite Christians and protected that church against imperial pressure, sponsoring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and monasteries. Their camp at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabiyah">Jabiyah</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan</a> and sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rusafa">Rusafa</a> served as courts, and poets such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nabigha-al-dhubyani">al-Nabigha</a> praised them.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 582 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> arrested <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mundhir-ibn-al-harith">al-Mundhir ibn al-Harith</a> and the federation broke up into rival chiefs. Revived partly against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>, Ghassanid forces fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-yarmuk">Yarmuk</a> in 636 against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>. Their last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabala-ibn-al-ayham">Jabala ibn al-Ayham</a>, briefly converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, then withdrew to Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ghassanid-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ghassanid Kingdom" width="320" height="276"><figcaption>Image: MoeyElan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghassanid_Influence_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>220 CE – 638 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jabiyah</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>al-Harith ibn Jabala, al-Mundhir ibn al-Harith, Jabala ibn al-Ayham</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Miaphysite Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a>, <a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a>, <a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>, <a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ghassanids, Ghassan, Banu Ghassan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=429&amp;focus=ghassanid-kingdom" aria-label="Ghassanid Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5602 979 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ghassanid Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5922 1235L5709 970M5922 1235L6053 1533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M6053 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5922 1235h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5922 1235h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Jabiyah. <a href="/atlas?year=429&amp;focus=ghassanid-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
